+  // six for either CKRL as well, because section 6.2.1 puts the prescaler ahead of the
+  // CPU/peripheral split, so it scales both nets by the same M.  A divisor stated against
+  // this clock therefore divides by M for free and must not consult ckrl_divider() itself.
+  virtual int fclk_periph_per_cycle(void);
+
+  // M of doc4235 section 6.2.1: 1 for CKRL = FFh (bypass, the reset value), else
+  // 2*(255-CKRL).  Applied once, in clock_per_cycle(), because FCLK_CPU and FCLK_PERIPH are
+  // the same net; anything that counts machine cycles (timers, PCA, watchdog, BRG, SPI) must
+  // NOT multiply by it, and anything stated in oscillator clocks either counts in
